# RULES FOR AI AGENT (ANTIGRAVITY)

## 1. UI SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH
- **MANDATORY**: You must usage `src/shared/components/ui/NeoComponents.tsx` for ALL UI elements.
- **PROHIBITED**: Do NOT use raw HTML tags like `<button>`, `<input>`, `<select>`, `<textarea>`, `<h1>`, `<p>`, `<span>` for UI components.
- **PROHIBITED**: Do NOT create new CSS classes or stylesheets unless absolutely necessary and approved. Use Tailwind utility classes via `className` prop on NeoComponents.
- **MAPPING**:
  - `<button>` -> `<NeoButton>`
  - `<input>` -> `<NeoInput>`
  - `<select>` -> `<NeoSelect>`
  - `<textarea>` -> `<NeoTextarea>`
  - `<div>` (card-like) -> `<NeoCard>`
  - Text tags -> `<Typography>`
  - Loading -> `<Spinner>`

## 2. COMPONENT USAGE GUIDELINES
- Always import `NeoComponents` from `src/shared/components/ui/NeoComponents`.
- Use `Typography` variants (`h1`...`h6`, `body`, `caption`, `label`) instead of heading tags.
- Use `NeoButton` variants (`primary`, `secondary`, `ghost`, `link`, `icon`, `glass`, `gradient`, `glow`) appropriate for the context.
- Use `NeoInput` and `NeoSelect` for all forms.

## 3. TEXT & CONTENT
- Prefer using constants from `src/shared/lib/constants.ts` for user-facing text strings (titles, labels, messages).
- Ensure all text is in Portuguese (pt-BR).

## 4. ERROR HANDLING
- Ensure `ConfigGuard` wraps the application to catch environment/connection errors.
- Fail gracefully with user-friendly messages.
